  {
    "id": "b8ef461d7b423307f537",
    "source": "Consumables go through use_item: it checks the character carries the item and can act, rolls and applies a healing potion's healing itself, and uses it up, all in one call; in a fight it is the user's action on their own turn, and feeding a potion to someone needs them within 5 feet. A character at 0 HP uses nothing. A charged item (a wand, a staff) goes through use_item with the spell it casts named in spell: the server sets the charge cost and the spell's level and spends the charges, and the item is kept and refills at dawn by itself. A spell scroll goes through use_item as well: the server refuses a scroll the reader cannot read (and the scroll is kept) and rolls the check for one above their level. Then cast that spell ONCE with the spell's own tool, the user as its caster: the server spends no slot for it and uses the item's save DC and attack bonus; a second cast of it spends a slot as usual. Attuning to a magic item takes a short rest; GAME STATE shows it as attuning until then.",
    "sourceHash": "b8ef461d7b423307f537e94b0652655b0e90b12e40584ce60f75e39f0f977b0a",
    "kinds": [
      "display-property"
    ],
    "sites": [
